Bugfixes:
 - We have a few SKIPIF instructions meant to skip an ADDPCI/SUBPCI that could not be applied if we generate multiple of those.
 - Ensure "const = const" style assignments don't strcpy.
 - Ensure "return simplestr" style assignments don't strcpy.
 - Only allow const[str] return type when truly returning a constant string (global const or string const or a const variable assigned from either).
 - Update "is_const" check in function return, it needs to check the function is a const also.
 - Ensure function calls to const str get their own local copy if it isn't a const or simple string.

General TODO:
 - Need to write up a langauge specification.

Optimizations that would be nice to have:
 - load/store purpose tracking, so redundant loads/stores and moves can be tracked.
 - ensure that loads which get overridden by another load or operation get removed.

Things that would be nice to have for convenience:
 - asm() block to allow inlining assembly.
 - auto-infer types for variables that can be inferred.
 - walrus operator, except in return statements.

Things that would be good for a complete compiler that I probably will not need:
 - 8/16/32 bit signed division.
 - 8/16/32 bit signed modulo.
 - 8/16/32 bit exponentiation.
 - variable pointer support.
 - function pointer support.
 - integer/boolean array support, including reading/writing values using array syntax.
 - support for allocating local and global arrays using int[length].
 - support for allocating extern global arrays using int[inf] or similar syntax.

Things that might become necessary if we run out of space in the boot ROM:
 - link-time duplicate instruction chain finder, replace with LNGJUMP to save on space.
 - link-time replace LNGJUMP with JRI when appropriately small jumps exist.
